1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,500
This is TiHiY StreamControl Center. It is a desktop API client for a content creator to manage their own YouTube live stream using YouTube API Services.

2
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:32,200
Step one: OAuth authorization. I open Channels. This is YouTube OAuth for a Desktop application. The redirect URI is 127.0.0.1 port 17847. The only OAuth scope requested is youtube.force-ssl.

3
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:56,900
I click Authorize and complete Google consent as the creator. After login, the client calls channels.list with mine=true. Here is the authenticated YouTube channel title and the channel URL. All later API calls use this signed-in account.

4
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:37,800
Step two: broadcast data retrieval. I open YouTube Broadcast. I click Refresh list. This list is liveBroadcasts.list with mine=true. Here you see the broadcast title, life cycle status live, privacy, and the watch URL.

5
00:01:52,030 --> 00:02:06,000
On the main console, live statistics come from videos.list, parts liveStreamingDetails and statistics: concurrent viewers and like count.

6
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:24,400
Step three: real-time chat. Incoming messages are liveChatMessages.list. The user interface shows the author's display name, the message text, and the author's YouTube channel URL.

7
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:45,800
I send a message with the YouTube button. This is liveChatMessages.insert as the authenticated creator. End result: the message appears in live chat.

8
00:02:53,980 --> 00:03:01,000
I delete that message. This is liveChatMessages.delete. End result: the message is removed from chat.

9
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:26,700
Moderation timeout. The confirmation dialog identifies the target YouTube channel name and channel URL, and the acting YouTube account name and channel URL. This call is liveChatBans.insert, temporary.

10
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:48,700
Permanent ban. The same dialog identifies the target channel and the acting account. This is liveChatBans.insert, permanent. End result: the test channel is banned from this live chat.

11
00:03:56,930 --> 00:04:06,400
Unban. This is liveChatBans.delete. The dialog again shows the target and acting channel URLs. End result: the ban is removed.

12
00:04:14,570 --> 00:04:27,800
Final result: this API client uses YouTube API Services only for the authenticated creator's own live broadcast, statistics, real-time chat, and moderation.
